IMAGE RULES (CRITICAL — broken images destroy the demo):
- These 6 URLs are the ONLY <img> src values allowed. NEVER invent paths like "logo.png", "images/hero.jpg", or any other URL.
- The brand logo must be TEXT (styled brand name in the design system font/color) — never an <img> logo.
- Icons must be inline SVG — never icon image files.
- Every image needs object-fit:cover and a fixed-height container so it never distorts.

═══ TECH STACK (MANDATORY) ═══
- Include in <head>: <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
- Style EVERYTHING with Tailwind utility classes. Do NOT hand-write CSS except: the Google Font import, a tailwind.config inline block setting the brand colors, and tiny keyframe animations if needed.
- Configure brand colors inline so you can use classes like bg-brand / text-brand:
  <script>tailwind.config = { theme: { extend: { colors: { brand: "PRIMARY_HEX", branddark: "DARKER_HEX" } } } }</script>
- Use the design system's font via Google Fonts + font-[name] classes or a body style.

═══ DESIGN QUALITY LAWS (breaking any of these = FAILED page) ═══
1. TEXT OVER IMAGES: text may only sit on a photo if there is a full-cover dark gradient overlay (e.g. bg-gradient-to-r from-black/70 to-black/30) and the text is white. NEVER put text in gray/translucent boxes floating on an image.
2. NO random background boxes behind headings. Headings sit directly on the section background.
3. HERO PATTERN (marketing pages): full-width section, image as absolute inset-0 cover + gradient overlay, content in a max-w-7xl container aligned LEFT with: small uppercase badge, huge bold white headline (text-5xl/6xl font-extrabold), 1-2 line gray-200 subtitle, two buttons (solid brand + outline white), then a social-proof row. Height ~85vh, content vertically centered. NO giant empty areas.
4. SECTION RHYTHM: every marketing section = py-20/py-24, max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6, header block (uppercase brand-color label + text-3xl/4xl bold title + muted subtitle) then content grid. Alternate white / gray-50 backgrounds.
5. CARDS: bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6/p-8, hover:shadow-lg transition. Images inside cards: h-48 w-full object-cover rounded-t-2xl.
6. BUTTONS: consistent — solid: bg-brand text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-branddark; outline: border-2 border-current px-6 py-3 rounded-full.
7. NAV: sticky top-0 bg-white/90 backdrop-blur border-b, brand name text logo left, links center/right, CTA button. Active link in brand color.
8. CONTRAST: body text gray-700 on white, never light-on-light or dark-on-dark. Test every text/background pair.
9. DASHBOARDS: grid layout with fixed dark sidebar (bg-slate-900, w-64), white content area bg-gray-50, stat cards with big numbers + trend badges, tables with avatars and status pills, SVG/div charts.
10. DENSITY: 250+ lines of HTML. Every section from the spec fully populated with realistic data (names, dates, metrics). No empty stretches taller than 80px.

BUILD RULES:
1. Implement EVERY section in the page spec — name, layout, components, and sample data exactly as described
